    {
      "kind": "legalText",
      "id": "beneficiary_rights_text",
      "text": "I have received, and the hospice has explained to me, a written notice of my rights as a hospice patient. The notice explains my rights, including the right to be informed of my rights before care is furnished; to be treated with dignity and respect; to have my person and property respected; to take part in planning my care; to choose my attending physician; to refuse care or treatment; to voice grievances without discrimination or reprisal; and to have my records kept confidential. The hospice has also given me information about its policies on advance directives.",
      "cite": "42 CFR 418.52(a)"
    },
